Google wants AI Mode in Search to answer with your own details in mind. On 23 November 2026 the company said it was starting to roll out an opt-in connection for Google Wallet, and that Google Drive will follow. This guide covers what is arriving, what Google says the connection can and cannot do, and what to check before you switch it on.

*Disclosure: this post was drafted by Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic, which competes with Google in AI products, and checked by a separate AI reviewer against the cited pages for figures, dates and wording. This is not a full human review. Stackbrook did not test the feature and has no affiliate relationship with Google at the time of writing. The header image is AI-generated.*

## What Google announced

The feature sits inside what Google calls Personal Intelligence, an optional setting that lets its AI tools draw on your connected apps. Gmail, Calendar and Photos are already part of it. The new post sets out these additions:

- **Google Wallet** started rolling out on 23 November as an opt-in connection in AI Mode.
- **Google Drive** is due in the coming weeks, so AI Mode can use context from your documents, spreadsheets or PDFs.
- **The Gemini app** is also due to share context with AI Mode, and you will be able to opt in to connect it to Personal Intelligence there.
- **A Personalization icon** is listed as coming soon, under tailored answers, to show which context AI Mode used. Google says you can correct it by telling AI Mode what has changed.

Google's examples for Wallet include planning financial milestones, finding ways to cut everyday spending, and getting more from cash-back categories, travel perks and reward points on cards linked through Wallet. For Drive, it suggests building a preparation plan ahead of tax season. These are the company's examples, not results we have checked.

![Table chart showing which Google apps connect to AI Mode and the status Google gives for each](/images/site1/google-ai-mode-wallet-drive-connect-explained-chart.svg)
